# Protected paths for merge-content gates (Lesson 1 from AutoCraft deep study).
# Files matching any of these patterns trigger a merge-content gate:
# they cannot be auto-merged under yolo without a recorded second-look verdict.
#
# Format: one glob pattern per line. Lines starting with # are comments.
# Empty lines are ignored. Patterns are matched against the diff paths
# (the path component after the two leading tabs in a git diff --name-only output).
#
# Global list is this file. Per-project override is
# config/protected-paths in the project's own worktree (read by
# fm_protected_paths_list in bin/fm-protected-paths-lib.sh when present).
#
# The list is the union of AutoCraft's "content a person looks at" gates
# and Firstmate's safety boundaries.

